  "language": "en",
  "text": "Raise your septic prices a little. Your customer won't feel it, but your margin will. I met with a client today whose investors gave them a list of changes and one of them was raising prices. They walked me through the list and I told them honestly that these were good changes, especially the price increase. A small increase barely registers with the customer. I promise you, if they can already pay hundreds of dollars they can pay a little bit more without even feeling it. Over a year it becomes the cushion that carries you through surprises. Margin isn't greed, it's how you get through the month, the truck breaks down. If you've been putting off a price increase you're not crazy for being nervous but it's probably the first thing I'd look at.",
